# NPClaude speech: the format, speech styles and building blocks. Lines for each topic are in the other
# .speech files beside this one (conversation, gifts, remarks, combat, brawls, family, words).
#
# Each "== name ==" is a symbol; each line under it is one way to say it. [name] fills in another symbol, a fact
# or a word. Braces at the end hold conditions: a pole (polite, polite+ for strongly), a quirk (glutton), a fact
# (time=night), any of them negated with "!", and w=2 to make a line more likely. Lines with more conditions are
# picked more often when they fit, so every symbol keeps plain lines as a fallback.
#
# Facts: name, listener, listener_type (player/npc), opinion (enemy/disliked/neutral/friendly/friend/close_friend),
# relation (ally/neutral/hostile: how they'd treat the listener in a fight),
# age (baby 0-2, child 3-9, young_teen 10-15, teen 16-17, adult; see ages.speech), birthday (yes on their birthday), relationship (single/dating/engaged/married/widowed), listener_kin (what the listener is to them: spouse, fiance,
# partner, parent, child, sibling, grandparent, grandchild, aunt_uncle, niece_nephew, cousin, ..._in_law, or none),
# to_partner (yes when the listener is their partner), listener_age (the listener's age stage),
# leader (yes/no), time (morning/day/evening/night), weather (clear/rain/snow/storm/fog/blood_rain), wet (yes when
# it's coming down on them), outside, season (spring/summer/fall/winter), biome (plains, desert, tundra...),
# climate (cold/mild/hot here), home_climate, home_biome and at_home (where they're from and whether they're there),
# weather_like/season_like/biome_like (love/like/meh/dislike/hate), mood (awful/bad/okay/good/great),
# health (fine/hurt/low), recovering (yes/no), has_faction, has_enemy, address, catchphrase.
# Words: taught_food, taught_animal, taught_thing, taught_place, taught_exclamation, taught_greeting,
# taught_farewell, taught_describe, taught_activity, taught_angry, taught_happy, taught_sad, taught_scared (words
# players taught them), partner, kin_call (Mom, Dad, Grandma, Grandpa, or the listener's name), favorite_food, hated_food, favorite_thing, hated_thing, weather_word, biome_word, season_word,
# favorite_weather, hated_weather, favorite_biome, hated_biome, favorite_season, hated_season, home_biome, faction,
# enemy_faction, and per event: enemy, food, item.
# Gifts add kind (food/valuable/junk/gross/material/tool/weapon/armor/flower/plant/curio/music/decor/dangerous/
# comfort/fun/block/item), taste, rude_gift (yes for dirt and the like) and surprising (yes when they feel very
# differently about it than most people would).
# Word modifiers: .a .the .s .it .is .this .cap

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speech style pools: rolled once per NPC.

== style_address ==
friend
friend                       {polite}
traveler                     {proper}
stranger                     {introvert}
pal                          {lighthearted}
mate                         {crude}
bud                          {crude, lighthearted}
chief                        {lighthearted}
my friend                    {proper, polite}
kid                          {rude}
buddy                        {extrovert}

== style_catchphrase ==
Cube God willing.            {pious, w=3}
Cube God keep you.           {pious, w=2}
Mark my words.               {proud}
Just saying.
Don't quote me on that.      {liar}
Honest truth.                {honest}
Could be worse.              {pessimist}
Could be better, too.        {pessimist}
Onward!                      {optimist}
Chin up.                     {optimist}
Ha!                          {lighthearted}
Heh.                         {lighthearted}
Anyway.
Funny old world.
Such is life.                {serious}
No rest for the wicked.      {hardworking}
Let's not rush things.       {lazy}
Hm.                          {introvert}
Strange times.               {curious}
Watch your back.             {paranoid}
Easy does it.                {zen}

== style_filler ==
y'know                       {!proper}
I reckon                     {!proper+}
I suppose
eh                           {lighthearted}
mind you                     {proper}
honestly                     {!liar}
truth be told
see                          {crude}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Building blocks

== hello ==
Hello.
Hey.
Hi there.
Oh, hey.
Hey there!                   {extrovert}
Oh! Hi!                      {extrovert+}
Greetings.                   {proper}
Good day.                    {proper, polite}
Yo.                          {crude, lighthearted}
Oi.                          {crude+}
Hey, you.                    {rude}
[taught_greeting]!           {w=3}
[taught_greeting], [listener]! {w=3}
Ugh, you.                    {rude+}
Morning.                     {time=morning}
Good morning!                {time=morning, optimist}
Evening.                     {time=evening}
You're up late.              {time=night}
...Hm.                       {introvert+}

== hello_named ==
[hello]
Hey, [listener].
[listener]!                  {extrovert}
Oh, [listener]. Hello.       {polite}
Ah, [listener]. Good to see you. {proper, polite}
Hey, [address].
[listener]. What now?        {rude}
Look who it is.              {lighthearted}
Look who it is. [listener]!  {lighthearted, opinion=friend}

== exclaim ==
Whoa!
Hey!
Oh no!                       {timid}
Ha!                          {brave}
By the Cube!                 {pious}
Blast!                       {!proper}
Rats!                        {lighthearted}
Good grief!                  {proper}
[taught_exclamation]!        {w=3}
